#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:41
msgid "Will the fixes change my design or slow my store?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:44
msgid "Only “Visible focus states” has any visual effect — a high-contrast outline shown when an element is focused with the keyboard, which is exactly what WCAG requires. Performance impact is negligible: most fixes are PHP filters, and the rest load one small CSS/JS file only while enabled. No external requests, ever."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:49
msgid "If a fix conflicts with your theme"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:53
msgid "Switch it off — the change is removed immediately — and report the theme + fix combination in the <a>support forum</a> so we can improve compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:71
msgid "Does this plugin make my store legally compliant with the EAA or ADA?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:75
msgid "No automated tool can, and you should distrust any that claims to. This plugin gives you an honest starting point: detected issues to review, opt-in fixes for common WooCommerce problems, and a statement template. It is not legal advice."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:80
msgid "Does the European Accessibility Act apply to my store?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:83
msgid "The EAA has been enforceable across all 27 EU member states since June 28, 2025. It generally applies to e-commerce sites selling to EU consumers and requires WCAG 2.1 Level AA. Micro-enterprises are exempt: fewer than 10 employees <strong>and</strong> annual turnover under €2M. Whether it applies to you specifically is a legal question — ask a professional."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:88
msgid "Is this an accessibility overlay like UserWay or accessiBe?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:91
msgid "No. Overlays add a floating toolbar and scripts that mask problems without fixing the page; disability advocates and European regulators consider them inadequate. This plugin reports real issues in your markup and, only when you opt in, fixes the actual markup."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:96
msgid "Does any data leave my site? Do I need an account?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:99
msgid "No and no. The scan engine is bundled in the plugin, scans run in your own browser against your own pages, and results are stored in your own WordPress database. The free version makes zero external requests."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:104
msgid "Do I need WooCommerce? Which versions are supported?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:107
msgid "Yes — the plugin targets WooCommerce stores specifically. Requirements: WordPress 6.5+, WooCommerce 8.0+, PHP 7.4+."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:112
msgid "Why are all six fixes off by default?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:115
msgid "Because every theme is different and we never alter your store without explicit opt-in. Recommended flow: run a scan, enable one fix, spot-check your store, repeat. Each fix switches off just as instantly."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:120
msgid "What happens to my data if I remove the plugin?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:123
msgid "Deactivating keeps everything. Deleting the plugin from the Plugins screen removes the plugin’s database table and options. The generated Accessibility Statement page is a normal WordPress page and is never deleted automatically."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:128
msgid "Is there a Pro version?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:131
msgid "Not yet. The free version is complete on its own. A Pro tier (full-site crawling, scheduled scans, PDF audit reports, advanced WooCommerce fixes) is planned post-launch."
msgstr ""

