#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:161
msgid "Installation & activation"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:164
msgid "Go to <strong>Plugins → Add New</strong>, search for “Accessi Compliance Kit”, click <strong>Install Now</strong>, then <strong>Activate</strong>. (Or upload the zip via <strong>Plugins → Add New → Upload Plugin</strong>.)"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:165
msgid "On activation the plugin creates one database table for scan results and seeds its default settings. <strong>All fixes start OFF</strong> — activating changes nothing on your store’s front end."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:166
msgid "Find the plugin under <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:171
msgid "Recommended first-run flow"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:174
msgid "Run a scan of your home page from the <strong>Scan</strong> tab."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:175
msgid "Review the detected issues, starting with Critical and Serious."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:176
msgid "Enable one fix at a time in <strong>Settings</strong>, then spot-check your store."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:177
msgid "Generate the accessibility statement draft and edit it before publishing."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:178
msgid "Re-scan regularly — or turn on the weekly email reminder."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:186
msgid "Running a Scan"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:189
msgid "Scan from the admin page"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:192
msgid "Open <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility</strong> and go to the <strong>Scan</strong> tab."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:193
msgid "The URL field is pre-filled with your home page; paste any URL <strong>on your own site</strong> (other domains are rejected by design)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:194
msgid "Click <strong>Scan this page</strong>. The page loads in a hidden frame and is checked in your browser by the bundled axe-core engine — nothing is sent anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:195
msgid "Results appear grouped by severity. Expand a row to see the affected element’s HTML, the CSS selector, why it was flagged, and a link to remediation guidance."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:200
msgid "Scan from the front end"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:202
msgid "While browsing your store logged in as an admin, click <strong>Scan this page</strong> in the admin bar — it opens the Scan tab with the current URL pre-filled."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:206
msgid "Scan history"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:208
msgid "The <strong>History</strong> tab lists past scans (date, URL, status, per-severity counts). Click a row to reopen its full results. Results are stored in your own database and never leave your server."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:215
msgid "Understanding Results"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:218
msgid "The four severity levels"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:222
msgid "<strong>Critical</strong> — blocks some users completely (e.g. an image conveying information with no text alternative)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:223
msgid "<strong>Serious</strong> — makes a core task very difficult (e.g. form fields without labels)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:224
msgid "<strong>Moderate</strong> — causes real friction but usually has a workaround."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:225
msgid "<strong>Minor</strong> — polish-level problems still worth cleaning up."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:227
msgid "Work top-down: clear Critical and Serious issues first."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:232
msgid "Why “detected issues” and not “violations”?"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:234
msgid "Automated results always include findings that need human interpretation — for example contrast on decorative elements, or alternative text that exists but is unhelpful. We report what the engine detected and leave the judgment to you."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:238
msgid "What automated scans can and cannot find"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:240
msgid "Automated checkers — including the industry-standard axe-core engine this plugin bundles — reliably detect roughly a third to a half of WCAG issues. The rest (keyboard flows, meaningful alt text, content clarity, sensible focus order) need human judgment. Treat a clean scan as a good baseline, not proof of compliance."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:247
msgid "The Six Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:248
msgid "Enable each fix under <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility → Settings</strong>. Each is independent, off by default, and instant to switch off again. Recommended: enable one at a time and re-check your store."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:256
msgid "Create the statement page"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:259
msgid "Go to <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility</strong> and find the <strong>Accessibility Statement</strong> card."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:260
msgid "Click <strong>Create statement page</strong>. A WordPress page titled “Accessibility Statement” is created from an EAA-oriented English template, pre-filled with your site name, contact details, and the current date."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:261
msgid "If a statement page already exists, the plugin warns you instead of creating a duplicate; creating a fresh page is an explicit second action."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:266
msgid "Edit before you publish"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:268
msgid "Treat the generated page as a strong draft, not a finished statement. It contains placeholders — notably the compliance level you claim and the “known limitations” section — that only you can fill in truthfully."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:272
msgid "Where to link it"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:274
msgid "Link the published page from your site footer — most stores put it next to the privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:281
msgid "Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:284
msgid "Dashboard widget & admin-bar notice"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:286
msgid "The WordPress dashboard widget shows your last scan date and detected-issue counts by severity, with a link to the full results. An admin-bar notice appears when your most recent scan detected critical issues."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:290
msgid "Weekly email reminder (opt-in)"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:292
msgid "Enable it in <strong>Settings</strong> to get a weekly email nudging you to re-scan. It uses WP-Cron and your site’s normal mail configuration; no external service is involved."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:299
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:302
msgid "The scan times out or never finishes"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:304
msgid "The scanned page must load in an iframe from your own site. Security plugins or headers that block same-origin framing (<code>X-Frame-Options: DENY</code>, a strict <code>frame-ancestors</code> CSP) will prevent the scan — allow same-origin framing and retry. Scans also require you to be logged in as an admin; a scan fails if the URL redirects (e.g. to a login page)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:308
msgid "“This URL is not part of this site.”"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:310
msgid "By design the scanner only accepts URLs on your own domain. Check for a different subdomain, protocol, or a trailing typo."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:314
msgid "The menu item is missing"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:316
msgid "The plugin registers nothing until WooCommerce 8.0+ is active — check the Plugins screen for WooCommerce. The menu lives under <strong>WooCommerce → Accessibility</strong> and requires an administrator account."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:320
msgid "A fix doesn’t seem to do anything"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:322
msgid "Most fixes are invisible by design (screen-reader text, <code>alt</code>/<code>aria</code> attributes). Verify with your browser’s element inspector, or re-run a scan of the same page and compare detected-issue counts. Also check for full-page caching — purge the cache after toggling a fix."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:326
msgid "The scan reports issues from my theme or page builder"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:328
msgid "The scanner reports everything on the rendered page regardless of origin. The per-issue guidance describes what needs to change; changes to theme markup need to happen in the theme (or a child theme), not in this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:335
msgid "Privacy & Data"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:338
msgid "What the plugin stores — and what leaves your site"
msgstr ""

#: assets/js/src/guide/content.jsx:341
msgid "Zero external calls. The axe-core engine ships inside the plugin, scans run in your browser, and results live in your database. No telemetry, no CDN, no accounts, no API keys."
msgstr ""

